    "q-125550": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following is a $3\\times 2$ matrix?\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,F=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,G=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "- The matrix $E$ has $2$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $2\\times 3.$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- The matrix $F$ has $3$ rows and $2$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 2.$ $\\,✓$\n\n- The matrix $G$ has $3$ rows and $3$ columns. So, its dimensions are $3\\times 3.$ $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, only $F$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix.",
