      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14270828/assets/d624edaffd8c90de40041d419cf65bcf8f3af5d31c8d88d1123bd8f3d7555166.png)\n\nWhat is the length of the major axis of the ellipse given above?",
      "worked_solution": "The major axis is the longest diameter of the ellipse, which is the line segment bounded by the points $(-3,1)$ and $(5,1).$ So, the length of the major axis is $5-(-3)=8.$",
