    "q-74639": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$\\frac{2\\text{i}}{1-3\\text{i}}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The denominator is $1-3\\text{i}$ and its conjugate is $1+3\\text{i}.$ We multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $1+3\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2\\text{i}}{1-3\\text{i}} & =\\frac{2\\text{i}}{1-3\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1+3\\text{i}}{1+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\text{i}+6{\\text{i}}^{2}}{{1}^{2}-{3}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6(-1)+2\\text{i}}{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6+2\\text{i}}{1+9} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6+2\\text{i}}{10}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-6+2\\text{i}}{10}=-\\frac{6}{10}+\\frac{2}{10}\\text{i}=-\\frac{3}{5}+\\frac{1}{5}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
