    "q-97525": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Given that $X∼B(7,0.9),$ compute $P(X<6).$ Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(7,0.9),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{x})(0.9)^{x}(0.1)^{7-x}.\n$$\n\nComputing $P(X<6)$ will require us to compute $f(x)$ at $x=0,1,2,…,5.$ However, if we compute the complement $P(X\\ge 6)$ instead, then we will only have to compute $f(x)$ at $x=6,7,$ which will result in a much faster computation.\n\nComputing $P(X\\ge 6),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 6) & =P(X\\in \\{6,7\\}) \\\\  & =f(6)+f(7) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{6})(0.9)^{6}(0.1)^{7-6}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{7})(0.9)^{7}(0.1)^{7-7} \\\\  & =7(0.9)^{6}(0.1)+(0.9)^{7} \\\\  & ≈0.8503\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<6) & =1-P(X\\ge 6) \\\\  & ≈1-0.8503 \\\\  & =0.1497\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
