    "q-73426": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "What is the sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series if the $3$rd term is $36$ and the common ratio is $3?$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the $n$th term of a geometric sequence to determine ${a}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}{r}^{n-1} \\\\ 36 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{(3-1)} \\\\ 36 & ={a}_{1}\\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\ 36 & =9{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe sum of the first $N$ terms of a geometric series can be determined by the formula\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{{a}_{1}(1-{r}^{N})}{1-r}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, ${a}_{1}=4$ and $r=3.$ Substituting our values into the formula for ${S}_{N}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{4(1-{3}^{N})}{1-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{(-2)}(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & =-2(1-{3}^{N}) \\\\  & =2({3}^{N}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
