    "q-67160": {
      "dom_id": "questionContainer",
      "name": "Question 21",
      "problem": "An arithmetic series has the first term ${a}_{1}=2$, the $6$th term ${a}_{6}=22$, and the sum of the series is ${S}_{N}=288.$ Find the number of terms $N$ in the series.",
      "worked_solution": "To solve this problem, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series.\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d)\n$$\n\nSince we know two terms of the arithmetic series, we can find its common difference, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{6}-{a}_{1}}{6-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{22-2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{5} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${a}_{1}=2$, $d=4$, and ${S}_{N}=288$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 288 & =\\frac{N}{2}(2\\cdot 2+(N-1)\\cdot 4) \\\\ 288 & =\\frac{N}{2}(4+4N-4) \\\\ 288 & =\\frac{N}{2}(4N) \\\\ 288 & =2{N}^{2} \\\\ 144 & ={N}^{2} \\\\ N & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because $N$ can't be negative.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
